{"name":"Cyberspace","hex":"#44484d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cyberspace","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A world of information accessed through the Internet.","The Internet as a whole."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cyberspace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cyberspace","blocks":[{"text":"Cyberspace is an interconnected digital environment. It is a type of virtual world popularized with the rise of the Internet. The term entered popular culture from science fiction and the arts but is now used by technology strategists, security professionals, governments, military and industry leaders and entrepreneurs to describe the domain of the global technology environment, commonly defined as standing for the global network of interdependent information technology infrastructures, telecommunications networks and computer processing systems. Others consider cyberspace to be just a notional environment in which communication over computer networks occurs. The word became popular in the 1990s when the use of the Internet, networking, and digital communication were all growing dramatically; the term cyberspace was able to represent the many new ideas and phenomena that were emerging.\nAs a social experience, individuals can interact, exchange ideas, share information, provide social support, conduct business, direct actions, create artistic media, play games, engage in political discussion, and so on, using this global network. Cyberspace users are sometimes referred to as \"cybernauts\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Chongqing_Nightscape.jpg/330px-Chongqing_Nightscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyberspace"},{"title":"Cyberspace (role-playing game)","blocks":[{"text":"Cyberspace is a near-future cyberpunk role-playing game published by Iron Crown Enterprises (I.C.E.) in 1989 using a revised set of rules from their previously published Space Master role-playing game."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cc/CyberspaceRPGCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyberspace_(role-playing_game)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"cyberspace":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cyberspace.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/00/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cyberspace.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cyberspace.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/00/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cyberspace.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cyberspace.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"65th Cyberspace Squadron Inactivation Ceremony (9087641)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/65th_Cyberspace_Squadron_Inactivation_Ceremony_%289087641%29.jpg/500px-65th_Cyberspace_Squadron_Inactivation_Ceremony_%289087641%29.jpg","ratio":1.3998357963875205,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:65th_Cyberspace_Squadron_Inactivation_Ceremony_(9087641).jpg","share":0.414375},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating.jpg","share":0.33125},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"